# ── Dependencies + build noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.payload.tmp
dashboard/assets/js/dist/*.map
# Render-probe screenshots. A probe writes these beside itself as evidence for ONE run;
# they are regenerated on demand and none of them is a record worth committing. The README
# screenshot is deliberately NOT here -- it lives in docs/ and is committed on purpose.
tools/probes/*.png

# ── Per-machine, never shared ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Rolling per-session development hand-off. Regenerated locally each session.
chronicle/next-chunk.md

# ── Not distributed, by decision ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Wallach book texts. These are their authors' copyrighted work and are NOT
# published here. They are kept locally for the corpus derive and for the two
# book-anchored gates; a fresh clone runs without them and those gates skip with
# a clear reason. See eden/corpus/README.md.
eden/corpus/books/*.txt

# Page scans of those same books, used only to verify OCR locally.
temporary/

# Wallach material recorded in full but deliberately held out of the app and out
# of the published repository. Kept on disk for review; nothing in the app or the
# gates reads it.
eden/fringe-knowledge/

# A pinned browser engine, if one is ever installed here. Absent by decision — a
# modern engine is 340-420 MB on disk, so it must never reach git.
engine/

# The packaged WEBSITE build (tools/build_web.py). Derived entirely from dashboard/,
# regenerated in one command, and ~36 MB — so it is built, not committed.
dist-web/

# The upload bundle built from dist-web/. Same reasoning: derived, regenerated in one command.
dist-web.zip

# The USDA FoodData Central SR Legacy archive (eden/foods/). Public-domain US
# government data, but 6 MB of zipped CSV that is re-downloadable in one command
# from the URL + sha256 pinned in eden/foods/usda-source.json. The byte-exact
# EXTRACT of the rows this app actually uses IS committed, so the composition
# gate runs on a fresh clone; the full archive is only needed to re-derive.
eden/foods/*.zip

# ── Outside food-composition source PAYLOADS (eden/foods/sources/) ───────────
# Same policy the seven Wallach books run under: the BYTES stay out of the repo, the
# NUMBERS we extracted are committed. Two reasons, and only one of them is size:
#   1. COPYRIGHT. Powell 2005 is a Cambridge University Press PDF. Facts are not
#      copyrightable and the extracted values are ours to ship; the article is not.
#   2. WEIGHT. 27 MB of government spreadsheets and archives, all re-downloadable
#      from the URL + sha256 pinned in eden/foods/sources/sources.json.
# Every extractor reads a payload if present and the committed extraction if not, so a
# fresh clone works with nothing downloaded.
eden/foods/sources/**/*.zip
eden/foods/sources/**/*.pdf
eden/foods/sources/**/*.xlsx
eden/foods/sources/**/*.xls
eden/foods/sources/**/*.csv
eden/foods/sources/**/*.xml
eden/foods/sources/**/*.html
